    {
      "id": "claim_645282df873944b4934b7a8d5a6494b2",
      "statement": "generate_assessment rejects with HTTP 409 if the user already has a ModuleTaskSession for the module in status 'passed' or 'in_progress', preventing duplicate active assessments or re-assessment after already passing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/api/src/agents/routers.py#L306-L333",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c941edb44de88a24184404fd6ae827f2b52867259c6de1d50597a226a484f1b2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c39d694616fc4652b5396e7c528a319d",
      "statement": "assessment_generator's persist_session node reuses an existing in_progress ModuleTaskSession by overwriting its generated_task when one exists for the user/module, and only creates a new ModuleTaskSession row otherwise; this is how a re-generated question after a failed attempt stays attached to the same session.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/agents/assessment_generator/nodes/persist_session.py",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:66861fd39496398877828ea4a91dd8d672e83f28b6e81b95c00ab29e812b5916"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_073e3b3b207f42cba0bf9c8f3f093d32",
      "statement": "evaluate_assessment re-checks that the session belongs to the requesting user and is in_progress, and blocks evaluation with HTTP 409 once the count of TaskAttempt rows with status evaluated for that session reaches Module.max_task_attempts.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/api/src/agents/routers.py#L359-L394",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6de448324e3d242b20681e1c8ccf28d35f331a063c4e9970fd15c001d1257399:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9f42b0fc03f049b68a3aec524a199720",
      "statement": "assessment_evaluator's evaluate_answer node prompts the LLM to return SCORE/PASSED/FEEDBACK, clamps the parsed score to 0-100, and recomputes is_passed in code as score >= passing_score rather than trusting the model's own PASSED field; the feedback prompt explicitly forbids revealing the correct answer.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/agents/assessment_evaluator/nodes/evaluate_answer.py#L8-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d2e380af06689b2007d5faf6070f77739c33e9694cffbe9a7ddb2a57d3ba8311:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_00de24368788469687919bae5af28523",
      "statement": "assessment_evaluator's persist_result node always inserts a new TaskAttempt with status evaluated, sets the session to passed if is_passed, and otherwise recounts evaluated attempts against Module.max_task_attempts to decide between leaving the session in_progress (attempts remain) or moving it to failed (cap reached).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/agents/assessment_evaluator/nodes/persist_result.py",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:fae3dd8e34ff302cfe508f389d776c15780b63db141c4ad8da46cd1c319b039a"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4d1a993d68074624bf4573b482187453",
      "statement": "AttemptStatus defines an 'error' member intended (per its inline comment) for API failures that should not count as a consumed attempt, but no node in assessment_evaluator currently sets it; instead the EvaluationService raises ValueError on any state['error'], which the router surfaces as HTTP 400.",
